  "id": "global-neuronal-workspace",
  "term": "global neuronal workspace",
  "definition": "Global neuronal workspace is a theory of consciousness that says a mental content becomes conscious when selected information is widely broadcast across the brain in a shared workspace. This broad access is proposed to let many otherwise nonconscious systems use the information, often with a rapid, large-scale “ignition” of brain activity when new information enters the workspace.",
